    "intro": {
      "type": "muto-lp-article",
      "settings": {
        "body": "<p>You read the labels and listened to the podcasts. You ended up with the names that keep coming up: NR, CoQ10, vitamin D3 with K2, a B complex, maybe zinc and resveratrol. <strong>You’ve been consistent for months.</strong> And you still can’t point at one pot and say “this is the one that’s working.”</p><p>That isn’t a discipline problem. It’s a design problem: doses you can’t see, ingredients sold one at a time, and no way to check any of it.</p><p>Here are seven reasons a cupboard of pots does less than it should, and why one daily protocol, two capsules with breakfast, can replace a good part of it.</p>",
        "band_main": "Rated 4.83 from 150+ reviews",
        "band_sub": "Made in the UK · Every batch third-party tested · 90 days to decide"
      }
    },
    "reasons": {
      "type": "muto-lp-reasons",
      "blocks": {
        "b1": {
          "type": "reason",
          "settings": {
            "title": "You’ve been taking it for months. You still can’t tell what’s working. Here’s why.",
            "body": "<p>A pot can list an ingredient without giving you a meaningful amount of it, and an all-in-one can list thirty ingredients at amounts too small to matter. The label has the name. You get a trace.</p><p>To take MUTO’s doses as separate products you’d need eleven pots on the kitchen side, every day. Nobody keeps that up for long, so the routine drifts, and then you blame yourself.</p><p><strong>You’re not inconsistent. The routine was never built to be checked.</strong></p>",
            "answer": "<p>Every dose is on the label: <strong>300mg NR</strong> (the most allowed in Great Britain), <strong>150mg CoQ10</strong>, 20mg PQQ, 50mg trans-resveratrol, 450mg TMG and 150mg grapeseed extract, with a full B complex, vitamin D3 and K2, zinc, copper and BioPerine®. Two capsules with breakfast.</p>",
            "answer_label": "The MUTO way"
          }
        },
        "b2": {
          "type": "reason",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Your body doesn’t use nutrients one at a time.",
            "body": "<p>Vitamin D3 and K2 belong together: both contribute to the maintenance of normal bones. The B vitamins work as a group: thiamin, riboflavin, niacin, B6 and B12 contribute to normal energy-yielding metabolism. Zinc and copper are balanced against each other.</p><p>Seven pots from seven brands were never designed to sit together. Nobody checked how they fit.</p>",
            "answer": "<p>MUTO was built as one formula: NR alongside TMG, D3 alongside K2, a full B complex, and BioPerine® in the same two capsules. One design, one label, chosen by a PhD cell biologist.</p>",
            "answer_label": "The MUTO way"
          }
        },
        "b3": {
          "type": "reason",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Proprietary blends hide the dose.",
            "body": "<p>If a label says “performance blend, 800mg”, you can’t tell whether the ingredient you bought it for is 400mg or 4mg. You can’t check it, and neither can your GP or your AI.</p><p><strong>If you can’t read the dose, you can’t judge the product.</strong></p>",
            "answer": "<p>No blends. All 19 ingredients and their doses are on the label. Paste it into your AI and ask what it thinks, or ask Richie: he answers formula questions himself.</p>",
            "answer_label": "The MUTO way"
          }
        },
        "b4": {
          "type": "cta",
          "settings": {
            "text": "Two capsules. Every dose on the label. 90 days to decide.",
            "label": "Start your 90 days",
            "link": "/products/muto-nad-cellular-complex"
          }
        },
        "b5": {
          "type": "reason",
          "settings": {
            "title": "You never took a starting point.",
            "body": "<p>Without a baseline there’s no verdict, just a feeling on a good week or a bad one. Most people start a new supplement on a Monday and judge it on a Thursday.</p><p>Single days are noise. Months are signal.</p>",
            "answer": "<p>Before your first capsule, rate how you feel at 3pm out of 10. If you wear a watch, note seven days of HRV, resting heart rate and sleep. Then compare at day 30 and day 90. Your numbers, your call.</p>",
            "answer_label": "The MUTO way"
          }
        },
        "b6": {
          "type": "reason",
          "settings": {
            "title": "You changed five things at once.",
            "body": "<p>New pot, new training plan, earlier nights, less wine. When something improves, you can’t say what did it, so you keep paying for all of it.</p>",
            "answer": "<p>One protocol in place of several pots means one clean change you can actually judge.</p>",
            "answer_label": "The MUTO way"
          }
        },
        "b7": {
          "type": "reason",
          "settings": {
            "title": "It costs more than you think.",
            "body": "<p>Bought separately at similar doses, MUTO’s main ingredients cost about <strong>£5.25 a day</strong> at UK retail: around £158 a month, across eleven pots and eleven reorders.</p>",
            "answer": "<p><strong>£2 a day</strong> on subscription. One jar, one delivery, and you can skip, pause or cancel online any time.</p>",
            "answer_label": "The MUTO way"
          }
        },
        "b8": {
          "type": "cta",
          "settings": {
            "text": "£5.25 a day bought separately. £2 a day in two capsules.",
            "label": "Start your 90 days",
            "link": "/products/muto-nad-cellular-complex"
          }
        },
        "b9": {
          "type": "reason",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Nobody stands behind it.",
            "body": "<p>Most supplement guarantees run 30 days, too short to judge anything. And when you have a question, there’s rarely a scientist on the other end.</p>",
            "answer": "<p><strong>90 days to decide.</strong> If you don’t see a difference, you’re covered on subscription. MUTO is built by Richie Barclay, a PhD cell biologist, and checked by our Scientific Advisory Board, and it’s being studied with four UK universities.</p>",
            "answer_label": "The MUTO way"
          }
        }
      },
